{"mod_id": "tfm2_transfer_fix", "name": "Transfer & Salary Fix", "author": "tfm2mods", "version": "0.2.2", "last_updated": "2026-11-25", "description": "Fixes two problems that push transfer fees and salaries far too high since the transfer system was rebuilt in game 0.7.0.\n\n1. AI asking price floor removed. In vanilla an AI team always asks at least 2.59x the base value when selling a player; with the mod the markup follows the market (usually around 1.25x). The negotiation floor and part of re-signing demands come down too.\n2. Safety cap on the salary / player value multiplier, which in vanilla compounds every year with no upper limit (default cap 5.0x). If salaries still climb too much, lower salary_mult_max (e.g. 3.0 or 2.0).\n\nOnly values calculated from now on change; contracts already signed stay as they are. It can be added at any point of a career, and turning it off returns both calculations to vanilla.\n\nSettings: tfm2_transfer_fix.cfg in the mod folder (created on first launch). Restart the game after editing.\n\nBuilt for game 0.7.4. The mod patches the game's own code, so it is rebuilt for each game update; on any other game version the game disables it, and the mod also checks the game code on startup and changes nothing if it does not match. Code mod (native DLL, Windows only).", "dependencies": [{"mod_id": "base", "version": ">=0.7.4, <0.7.5"}]}